# Log Locations

This file specifies where to check for logs when debugging issues.

## Docker Containers
backend: docker
frontend: docker

## Commands to Check Logs

### Backend Logs
```bash
docker-compose logs backend
docker-compose logs -f backend  # Follow logs in real-time
```

### Frontend Logs
```bash
docker-compose logs frontend
docker-compose logs -f frontend  # Follow logs in real-time
```

### Database Logs
```bash
docker-compose logs db
```

### Redis Logs
```bash
docker-compose logs redis
```

### Celery Worker Logs
```bash
docker-compose logs celery
```

### Celery Beat Logs
```bash
docker-compose logs celery-beat
```

### All Services
```bash
docker-compose logs
docker-compose logs -f  # Follow all logs
```

## Application Logs (Backend)

The backend creates log files in `backend/logs/` directory:
- `django.log` - General application logs
- `errors.log` - Error-only logs (JSON format)
- `security.log` - Auth/permissions warnings
- `api.log` - API-specific operations
- `celery.log` - Background task logs
- `database.log` - SQL queries (DEBUG mode only)

Check these files when debugging backend issues:
```bash
tail -f backend/logs/django.log
tail -f backend/logs/errors.log
tail -f backend/logs/api.log
```
